    "Now I have a complete picture of the project. Let me produce the full strategy.\n\n---\n\n# Nexus Protocol — Complete Leaderboard Growth Strategy\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1 — Project Audit\n\n### Current Architecture Summary\n\n| Layer | What Exists | State |\n|---|---|---|\n| Smart Contract | `lending-pool.clar` (v1 + v2) | Minimal: deposit/withdraw/borrow/repay only |\n| Frontend | React + WalletConnect (App.jsx) | Only deposit UI wired; borrow/repay/withdraw missing |\n| Secondary Component | `LendingpoolInterface.jsx` | Points at testnet, broken, unused |\n| Interaction Scripts | `interact.ts`, `loop-txs.ts` | Working but manual/single-user |\n| SDK/API | `stacks-api.ts`, `monitoring.ts` | Built but not connected to frontend |\n| Tests | Vitest + Clarinet SDK | Config present, no test files visible |\n\n### Strengths\n- Live on mainnet with a real contract address\n- Working deposit/withdraw/borrow/repay cycle — a complete DeFi primitive\n- `loop-txs.ts` already demonstrates automated cycling\n- Stacks.js SDK properly integrated\n- Clean contract logic, no obvious exploits\n\n### Weaknesses\n\n**Critical:**\n- Frontend only exposes `deposit` — users cannot borrow, repay, or withdraw from the UI\n- `LendingpoolInterface.jsx` points at testnet with a wrong contract address — dead code\n- No read-only data displayed (pool stats, user balance, loan status) — users are blind\n- WalletConnect setup is fragile (modal re-created on every call, `stx_signTransaction` vs `stacks_contractCall` mismatch)\n- No wallet connection via Stacks Connect (Leather/Xverse) — the standard for Stacks dApps\n\n**Growth:**\n- Zero engagement loops — one action (deposit) and users leave\n- No daily reason to return\n- No social sharing, referrals, or community hooks\n- No on-chain events/print statements — no activity feed possible\n- No streak, XP, or reward system\n- No leaderboard or social proof\n\n**Gas:**\n- `loop-txs.ts` uses 20,000 µSTX (0.02 STX) per tx — 10x higher than minimum needed\n- `interact.ts` uses 3,000 µSTX — still 3x higher than minimum\n- No batching — every action is a separate transaction\n\n### Missing Growth Loops\n1. No reason to return after first deposit\n2. No social proof (no \"X users deposited today\")\n3. No gamification layer\n4. No referral mechanism\n5. No lightweight interactions (check-in, vote, react) that cost <0.001 STX\n6. No notifications or reminders\n\n---\n\n## Phase 2 — Leaderboard Gap Analysis\n\n### Gap to Top 50\n\n| Metric | Current | Target (rank ~33) | Gap | Multiplier Needed |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Transactions | 482 | 11,000 | 10,518 | 23× |\n| DAU | 6 | 2,000 | 1,994 | 333× |\n| Gas Spent | 9.57 STX | 19.60 STX | 10.03 STX | 2× |\n\n### Highest ROI Metric: Transactions\n\nDAU growth requires real user acquisition (hard, slow). Transactions can be multiplied by:\n1. Adding more interaction surfaces per user (each user does 5–10 actions/day instead of 1)\n2. Deploying ultra-cheap engagement contracts (check-in, streak, vote) that cost 0.001–0.003 STX each\n3. Fixing the frontend so users can complete full borrow/repay cycles (4 txs per cycle vs 1)\n\n### Expected Transaction Output with 10 STX Budget\n\nAt 0.002 STX per tx (minimum viable fee on Stacks):\n- 10 STX ÷ 0.002 = **5,000 transactions maximum theoretical**\n- Realistic with overhead: **3,000–4,000 transactions**\n\nWith 6 DAU doing 5 interactions/day for 7 days = 210 txs from existing users\nWith 50 new users doing 3 interactions/day for 7 days = 1,050 txs\n**Realistic 7-day target: 1,500–2,500 transactions** (bringing total to ~2,000–3,000)\n\n### Priority Ranking\n\n| Strategy | Impact | Speed | Gas Cost | Retention |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Fix full frontend (borrow/repay/withdraw) | High | 1 day | None | High |\n| Deploy check-in/streak contract | Very High | 1 day | 0.001/tx | Very High |\n| Add pool stats + user dashboard | Medium | 4 hours | None | High |\n| Deploy XP/reputation contract | High | 1 day | 0.001/tx | High |\n| Referral system | High | 2 days | 0.002/tx | Very High |\n| Community quest contract | Medium | 2 days | 0.001/tx | Medium |\n\n---\n\n## Phase 3 — System Design\n\n### System 1: Daily Check-in + Streak Contract\n\n**Architecture:** Single map tracking last check-in block per user. Streak counter incremented if check-in is within ~144 blocks (~24h). Costs one map-set write.\n\n**Gas estimate:** ~0.001–0.0015 STX per check-in (minimal state write)\n\n**Engagement impact:** Creates a daily reason to open the app. Streak loss anxiety drives retention. This is the single highest-ROI contract to deploy.\n\n```clarity\n;; nexus-checkin.clar\n(define-map streaks principal { last-block: uint, count: uint, total: uint })\n(define-map badges principal (list 10 uint))\n\n(define-constant BLOCKS-PER-DAY u144)\n(define-constant err-too-soon (err u200))\n(define-constant err-streak-broken (err u201))\n\n(define-read-only (get-streak (user principal))\n  (default-to { last-block: u0, count: u0, total: u0 } (map-get? streaks user))\n)\n\n(define-public (check-in)\n  (let (\n    (data (get-streak tx-sender))\n    (last (get last-block data))\n    (current stacks-block-height)\n    (gap (- current last))\n  )\n    (asserts! (>= gap u1) err-too-soon)\n    (let (\n      (new-count (if (and (> last u0) (<= gap (* BLOCKS-PER-DAY u2)))\n                   (+ (get count data) u1)\n                   u1))\n    )\n      (map-set streaks tx-sender {\n        last-block: current,\n        count: new-count,\n        total: (+ (get total data) u1)\n      })\n      (ok new-count)\n    )\n  )\n)\n```\n\n**Implementation complexity:** Low (1 day)\n\n---\n\n### System 2: XP / Reputation Contract\n\n**Architecture:** Map of principal → XP uint. Public functions award XP for protocol actions. Other contracts call `award-xp` via contract-call. Tiers computed read-only.\n\n**Gas estimate:** ~0.001 STX per award (one map-set)\n\n```clarity\n;; nexus-xp.clar\n(define-map xp-balances principal uint)\n(define-constant CONTRACT-OWNER tx-sender)\n(define-constant err-unauthorized (err u300))\n\n(define-read-only (get-xp (user principal))\n  (default-to u0 (map-get? xp-balances user))\n)\n\n(define-read-only (get-tier (user principal))\n  (let ((x (get-xp user)))\n    (if (>= x u1000) \"Diamond\"\n    (if (>= x u500)  \"Gold\"\n    (if (>= x u100)  \"Silver\"\n                     \"Bronze\")))\n  )\n)\n\n(define-public (award-xp (user principal) (amount uint))\n  (begin\n    (asserts! (is-eq contract-caller CONTRACT-OWNER) err-unauthorized)\n    (map-set xp-balances user (+ (get-xp user) amount))\n    (ok true)\n  )\n)\n```\n\n**Implementation complexity:** Low (half day)\n\n---\n\n### System 3: Referral Contract\n\n**Architecture:** Map of referrer → referred list. On first protocol interaction, user registers referrer. Referrer earns XP per successful referral. Anti-abuse: one referrer per address, self-referral blocked.\n\n**Gas estimate:** ~0.002 STX per referral registration\n\n```clarity\n;; nexus-referral.clar\n(define-map referrals principal principal)        ;; referred → referrer\n(define-map referral-count principal uint)        ;; referrer → count\n(define-constant err-already-referred (err u400))\n(define-constant err-self-referral (err u401))\n\n(define-read-only (get-referrer (user principal))\n  (map-get? referrals user)\n)\n\n(define-read-only (get-referral-count (referrer principal))\n  (default-to u0 (map-get? referral-count referrer))\n)\n\n(define-public (register-referral (referrer principal))\n  (begin\n    (asserts! (not (is-eq tx-sender referrer)) err-self-referral)\n    (asserts! (is-none (map-get? referrals tx-sender)) err-already-referred)\n    (map-set referrals tx-sender referrer)\n    (map-set referral-count referrer\n      (+ (get-referral-count referrer) u1))\n    (ok true)\n  )\n)\n```\n\n**Implementation complexity:** Low (half day)\n\n---\n\n### System 4: Lightweight Poll/Vote Contract\n\n**Architecture:** Protocol owner creates polls (stored as map of poll-id → options tuple). Users vote once per poll. Ultra-cheap: one map-set per vote.\n\n**Gas estimate:** ~0.001 STX per vote\n\n```clarity\n;; nexus-polls.clar\n(define-map polls uint { question: (string-ascii 100), option-a: uint, option-b: uint, active: bool })\n(define-map votes { poll: uint, voter: principal } bool)\n(define-data-var poll-count uint u0)\n(define-constant CONTRACT-OWNER tx-sender)\n(define-constant err-already-voted (err u500))\n(define-constant err-inactive (err u501))\n(define-constant err-unauthorized (err u502))\n\n(define-public (create-poll (question (string-ascii 100)))\n  (let ((id (var-get poll-count)))\n    (asserts! (is-eq tx-sender CONTRACT-OWNER) err-unauthorized)\n    (map-set polls id { question: question, option-a: u0, option-b: u0, active: true })\n    (var-set poll-count (+ id u1))\n    (ok id)\n  )\n)\n\n(define-public (vote (poll-id uint) (choice bool))\n  (let ((poll (unwrap! (map-get? polls poll-id) err-inactive)))\n    (asserts! (get active poll) err-inactive)\n    (asserts! (is-none (map-get? votes { poll: poll-id, voter: tx-sender })) err-already-voted)\n    (map-set votes { poll: poll-id, voter: tx-sender } true)\n    (map-set polls poll-id (merge poll {\n      option-a: (if choice (get option-a poll) (+ (get option-a poll) u1)),\n      option-b: (if choice (+ (get option-b poll) u1) (get option-b poll))\n    }))\n    (ok true)\n  )\n)\n```\n\n**Implementation complexity:** Low (half day)\n\n---\n\n### System 5: Quest Contract\n\n**Architecture:** Quests are milestones (e.g., \"deposit 3 times\", \"check in 7 days\"). Completion tracked per user. Frontend reads quest state and shows progress. Completion calls award-xp.\n\n**Gas estimate:** ~0.002 STX per quest completion\n\n```clarity\n;; nexus-quests.clar\n(define-map completed-quests { user: principal, quest: uint } bool)\n(define-constant QUEST-FIRST-DEPOSIT u1)\n(define-constant QUEST-STREAK-7 u2)\n(define-constant QUEST-REFER-FRIEND u3)\n(defi